From: pmOS Q706F fixes
Subject: [PATCH] HID: i2c-hid: override Q706F folio Elan 04F3:31F3 descriptors

The pogo touchpad at i2c-9 addr 0x60 returns a zero-length HID report
descriptor over I2C, so hid-multitouch never binds. Android DTBO 0x30d08
hardcodes the 30-byte HID descriptor and 383-byte report descriptor;
reuse those blobs on lenovo,q706f.

---
--- a/drivers/hid/i2c-hid/i2c-hid-dmi-quirks.c	2026-08-29 14:19:31.000000000 +0800
+++ b/drivers/hid/i2c-hid/i2c-hid-dmi-quirks.c	2026-10-09 10:38:38.361910768 +0800
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/dmi.h>
 #include <linux/hid.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 
 #include "i2c-hid.h"
 #include "../hid-ids.h"
@@ -290,6 +291,84 @@
 };
 
 
+
+/*
+ * Lenovo Xiaoxin Pad Pro 12.6 (Q706F) folio Elan 04F3:31F3 @ i2c-9 0x60.
+ * Android DTBO board-id 0x30d08 ships hid-descr-preset + hid-report-descr-preset
+ * because the IC returns zeros over I2C for both descriptors. Mainline i2c-hid
+ * only has a DMI override path; match OF compatible instead.
+ */
